.\" vyk(1) — man page for the vyakarana CLI
.\" Format: groff_man(7).  Render with `man -l docs/man/vyk.1`
.\"           or `groff -man -Tutf8 docs/man/vyk.1 | less -R`.
.\"
.\" Update procedure: this page mirrors `vyk --help` (src/main.cyr
.\" `print_help`).  When changing one, refresh the other and the
.\" 1.13.1 smoke probes.
.\"
.TH VYK 1 "2026-05-08" "vyakarana 1.13.1" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
vyk \- source-code tokenizer (vyakarana demo CLI)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B vyk
[\fIOPTIONS\fR]
[\fIFILE\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B vyk
reads
.I FILE
and emits one NDJSON record per recognized token, or ANSI-coloured
source bytes when
.B \-\-theme=
is given.
.PP
Detection is automatic: extension first
.RI "(" .sh ", " .py ", " ".rs," " ...),"
content sniff for extensionless files (shebang, BOM, magic
bytes), and an asm flavour vote for
.IR .s / .S .
Override with
.B \-\-language=<name>\fR.
.PP
Without
.IR FILE ,
.B vyk
prints help and exits 0.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print help and exit.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Print version and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-list-kinds
Print the ten token kinds and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-list-languages
Print every loaded grammar name and exit.
.TP
.BI \-\-language= name
Override extension/content detection. Run
.B \-\-list-languages
for valid names.
.TP
.BI \-\-theme= name
Render ANSI-coloured source instead of NDJSON. Bundled themes:
.BR default ", " dark ", " none .
See
.I docs/architecture/004-theme-palette-contract.md
for the kind\(->slot mapping.
.TP
.BI \-\-export-theme= format
Emit a theme file for the named editor format and exit. Formats:
.BR vscode " (theme.json),"
.BR helix " (theme.toml),"
.BR iterm " (.itermcolors plist)."
Pair with
.B \-\-theme=<name>
to pick the source palette (default:
.BR default ).
.TP
.B \-\-handcoded
Route through the M1 hand-coded shell oracle. Regression
diagnostic for the shell grammar only.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
Tokenization produced one or more
.I error
token kinds (grammar gap or malformed input).
.TP
.B 2
Bad command-line usage. Run
.B \-\-help
for syntax.
.TP
.B 3
Cannot read
.IR FILE :
file not found or not readable.
.TP
.B 4
No grammar matched
.IR FILE .
Run
.B \-\-list-languages
to see all bundled names, then retry with
.B \-\-language=<name>\fR.
.SH EXAMPLES
NDJSON tokens to stdout:
.PP
.RS
.nf
\fBvyk script.sh\fR
.fi
.RE
.PP
ANSI-coloured render with the dark theme:
.PP
.RS
.nf
\fBvyk \-\-theme=dark file.rs\fR
.fi
.RE
.PP
Tokenize an extensionless script via explicit language:
.PP
.RS
.nf
\fBvyk \-\-language=python script\fR
.fi
.RE
.PP
Emit a VS Code theme file:
.PP
.RS
.nf
\fBvyk \-\-export-theme=vscode > theme.json\fR
.fi
.RE
.PP
Discover available grammar names:
.PP
.RS
.nf
\fBvyk \-\-list-languages | grep ml\fR
.fi
.RE
.SH OUTPUT
NDJSON records, one per line:
.PP
.RS
.nf
{"kind":"keyword","start":0,"len":2}
.fi
.RE
.PP
Where
.I kind
is one of:
.B ident, keyword, string, number, comment, operator,
.B punctuation, whitespace, preprocessor, error;
.I start
is a 0-indexed byte offset into
.IR FILE ;
and
.I len
is the token's byte length. Every input byte maps to exactly
one token's
.RI [ start ", " start + len )
span (the
.I coverage invariant\fR).
.SH FILES
.TP
.I dist/vyakarana.cyr
Single-file bundle for downstream
.BR cyrius (1)
consumers. Includes all 38 grammars inlined as Cyrius string
literals.
.TP
.I grammars/<name>.cyml
Source grammar definitions. Authored by hand, embedded by
.B scripts/embed-grammars.sh
into the bundle.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR cyrius (1),
.BR owl (1).
.PP
